========================================================================
6. Build tools — KAGE engine (GPL-3.0) and Potrace (GPL-2.0-or-later)
========================================================================
The Chinese hanzi were produced by rendering GlyphWiki's freely-licensed
skeleton data (section 2) into outlines with the KAGE engine
(https://github.com/MihailJP/kage-engine, GNU GPL v3) and then tracing the
result with Potrace (https://potrace.sourceforge.net/, GNU GPL v2 or later).

These are BUILD TOOLS. None of their program code is contained in or
distributed with the font files; the font stores only the resulting glyph
outlines, which are derived from the free GlyphWiki data, not from the tools'
source code.

This position rests on two grounds:

  (a) The GNU GPL version 3, section 0, states that "the output from running
      a covered work is covered by this License only if the output, given its
      content, constitutes a covered work." The Free Software Foundation's
      GPL FAQ likewise explains that the output of a program is generally not
      covered by the license of that program, unless the program copies part
      of itself into the output. The glyph outlines in this font are derived
      from GlyphWiki's freely-licensed skeleton data, not from the source
      code of KAGE or Potrace.

  (b) The same position is taken upstream. HZ Socho is generated in exactly
      the same way — KAGE engine and Potrace applied to GlyphWiki data — yet
      is released under the X11 terms in section 1 by the author of that very
      KAGE-engine fork.

On this basis this font is distributed under the permissive terms above
(sections 1-5) rather than the GPL.

Note: this is a good-faith reading of the upstream terms, not legal advice.
If you redistribute the *build scripts* together with a copy of the KAGE
engine or Potrace, keep those tools under their own GPL licenses.


========================================================================
7. Reserved name
========================================================================
Derivative fonts must not use "Insomnia" or "不寐" in their names.

This condition is imposed by the present author on his own contribution to
this font, and serves the same purpose as the "Reserved Font Name" mechanism
of the SIL Open Font License: to prevent modified versions from being
mistaken for official releases of this project.

It does not restrict, and is not intended to restrict, anyone's rights to the
upstream material described in sections 1-5 under those sections' own terms.


